    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's seen as a conspiracy theory but i mean, why go through the trouble of the 440hz standard specifically? it feels way too intentional. if you look at the math behind wave interference and how it affects brainwaves, it's not like it's impossible to influence a population's state through ambient resonance. isn't there any precedent for \"subliminal\" technical standards being used like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
