      "content": "okay but you said it's an \"engineering necessity\" for consistency. if the grid has to stay at one exact frequency to work, that means the frequency is actually being actively managed and adjusted constantly by centralized authorities to prevent deviation. if they have that much control over the frequency to keep the grid stable, wouldn't it be a tiny extra step to nudge it slightly to favor certain wave patterns? it seems like a huge vulnerability if you wanted to implement something like that on a mass scale.",
